  "question": {
    "id": 6,
    "label": "Problem 6",
    "statement": "Design a Turing machine that computes x + 3y in tally notation, reusing your earlier constructions. The tape starts with the y block on the left and the x block on the right, with the head on the rightmost stroke of the x block, and the machine must halt leaving a single block of x + 3y strokes in standard position.",
